re: 4.1.9.2
saw: 5e081cd5
ack: node
is: Premise 4.1.3.3 says Wasmtime builds on no_std without Cranelift and Winch and then runs precompiled code only; the refetched page adds that using Cranelift or Winch 'requires a host operating system which supports creating executable memory pages on-the-fly'. So Wasmtime does not assume std; its compilers are what a no_std host loses. The node should say 'Wasmtime's compilers, Cranelift and Winch, are left out of its no_std build and need an operating system that can make executable pages' in place of 'Cranelift and Wasmtime assume std and an operating system'.
